# Contacts of the people hyperactivity is for

Kept in the source and never served: the public server withholds every path under private/ (s-withheld,
lib/server.cub). Avik, 2026-11-18 12:20 UTC: "they should all have contact in the repo but it should not be
published on the website - and only if they already have a public facing email of course." So an address is
here only where the person (or their institution, on their own page) publishes it; the page it was read on
follows it. Each row's node in the workflow is reach-<name>; people-findable is the goal this serves.
Terence Tao is left out at Avik's word. Looked up 2026-11-18.

